[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue and one fix. Its reports hold two causes, and each now
has its own ticket:

| cause in #4471 | row in the desk's table | ticket |
|---|---|---|
| The shared parser reads dates month first | `parser` | [#1](https://github.com/promanowicz/megadev/issues/1) |
| The booking-v3 form hints MM/DD to day-first tenants | `hint` | [#2](https://github.com/promanowicz/megadev/issues/2) |

<Callout kind="warn">
Not known, not one fix. The queued parser fix closes only #1. The booking-v3 hint (#2) stays
broken after it ships.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds, as the desk counts it

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Each report is counted once, by its id, and each report is in exactly one ticket. The reports the
desk read as a one-day move are counted where the desk files them, under `parser`, so they are in
#1, with a note there.

## The two causes

### 1 · The shared parser reads dates month first · [#1](https://github.com/promanowicz/megadev/issues/1)

Every tenant on file writes the day first, and the shared parser reads every date month first, so
day and month swap: "4 March turned into 3 April". It hits every tenant, through the app, by
email and through the booking-v2 form. This is the problem #4471 describes.

A few of these reports describe a date that moved by one day, not a swap: "Invite says Tuesday
12 May. Calendar says Monday 11 May". The desk reads them as one-day moves and files them here by
tenant. Check them again once the parser fix ships.

### 2 · The booking-v3 form hints MM/DD · [#2](https://github.com/promanowicz/megadev/issues/2)

All of these reports came through the booking form of the three tenants on booking-v3
(alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour). The form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field,
so people type the month first, and the form then reads the date the tenant's way, day first. The
reports look like the parser's, but the cause is the hint. A parser fix does not touch it. The
table above marks this row "not this ticket — no ticket of its own": its ticket is now #2.

## Why they ended up in one ticket

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line. The same
  subjects, "Date is wrong" among them, occur under both causes, so both landed in #4471.
- The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser; the table above shows how often it
  disagrees with the cause. It cannot split the ticket.
- The split uses what the desk knows about the tenant (locale and booking form) and the channel.

## What to do

- Track each cause in its own ticket: [#1](https://github.com/promanowicz/megadev/issues/1),
  [#2](https://github.com/promanowicz/megadev/issues/2).
- Change the status of #4471 from known to split, and point it to this page.
- Before the next merge on subject, check the tenant and the channel: two reports with the same
  subject can have different causes.

